{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344118-perfected-material-armor","id":1344118,"title":"Perfected Material Armor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-27T21:09:59-07:00","id":1344118,"title":"Perfected Material Armor","content":"I was toying around with the notion of armor made out of perfected materials, and I noticed that there don't seem to be rules for what armor made out of them would count as.<br /> <br /> Siderite is the most obvious choice. You'd need to make it flexible (either via cunning joins and the like), but while it would itself resist all harm, the person underneath it would still have to deal with the impact of blows.<br /> <br /> If one had plate armor forged entirely of Siderite, what should its protective value be in terms of its Armor rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T21:50:37-07:00","id":1344125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344118-perfected-material-armor#post1344118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one had plate armor forged entirely of Siderite, what should its protective value be in terms of its Armor rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same as normal steel, but immune to armor piercing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T01:12:12-07:00","id":1344147,"title":"","content":"By the way, does an armor made of Dumamium has any use of its mana reserve? Can it soak aggravate damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T02:13:42-07:00","id":1344154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344118-perfected-material-armor?p=1344147#post1344147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, does an armor made of Dumamium has any use of its mana reserve? Can it soak aggravate damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the write up it can\u2019t soak Aggravated. Your Brawl while in it though could inflict Aggravated with the mana.<br /> <br /> Employ rule of cool or ask your ST as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T08:17:21-07:00","id":1344192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344118-perfected-material-armor#post1344118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was toying around with the notion of armor made out of perfected materials, and I noticed that there don't seem to be rules for what armor made out of them would count as.<br /> <br /> Siderite is the most obvious choice. You'd need to make it flexible (either via cunning joins and the like), but while it would itself resist all harm, the person underneath it would still have to deal with the impact of blows.<br /> <br /> If one had plate armor forged entirely of Siderite, what should its protective value be in terms of its Armor rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably need to clear it with your GM. Orichalcum cannot have its durability reduced by non-supernatural means, Siderite is harder than Orichalcum so I imagine the same. I would probably rule it as using the same rules as normal equipment but with that bonus plus immunity to armor piercing. That being said, there is a lot of room for experimentation.<br /> <br /> You don't necessarily need to stick to traditional armor. The outer shell could be a tri-weave fiber mesh dipped in an Orichalcum and Siderite alloy. That way you can benefit from the flexibility and chemical inertia of Orichalcum while still maintaining the protection of Siderite.<br /> <br /> Then you could add a magnetorheological fluid layer in between them, allowing for greater shock absorption. But instead of iron flakes suspended in oil, you use Siderite suspended in perfected oil. Of course, you will need to figure out how to supply the current to active it, but perfeing a battery and a conductor probably solves it.<br /> <br /> All this can be done without losing much in terms of flexibility. Use Matter to create a void between layers and you can probably make it resistant to extreme temperatures.<br /> <br /> The Adamantine Arrow would probably be very interested in developing something like this for emergencies, its likely the Free Council would love presenting this as a triumph of the Ars Nova. A crafting focused Legacy member (Forge Masters, Transhuman Engineers, etc) would probably talk your ear off, they almost certainly know of superior supernatural materials, occult principles and manufacturing techniques to take this idea to the next level. <br /> <br /> Of course, some mages take this idea, run with it and become Iron Man, the Doomslayer and more:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291687-new-legacy-the-clockwork-knights\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ckwork-knights</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-28-2019, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T03:02:37-07:00","id":1344621,"title":"","content":"Just add perfected leather shirt, it will completely absorb the kinetic energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://foru